  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the mapping:\n\n**Babel side** (`babel--v7.24.0`):\n- `packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts` \u2014 the dispatch point: `options.legacy || version === \"legacy\"` routes to the stage-2 legacy visitor; anything else (`2018-09`\u2026`2023-11`) routes into `createClassFeaturePlugin` (stage-3/TC39 semantics).\n- `packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/transformer-legacy.ts` \u2014 the legacy visitor itself (`applyClassDecorators`/`applyTargetDecorators`), which only wraps decorator calls (`applyDecoratedDescriptor`) around class members \u2014 it does **not** emit any `Reflect.metadata`/`design:type` data on its own.\n- `packages/babel-helper-create-class-features-plugin/src/decorators.ts` \u2014 stage-3 implementation shared by `2021-12`+ versions.\n- `packages/babel-plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts` + `packages/babel-preset-typescript/src/index.ts` \u2014 TS type-stripping plugin and how `preset-typescript` wires it in; critically, Babel's TS plugin strips type annotations but never reads them to synthesize metadata. Design-type emission (`emitDecoratorMetadata` parity) requires a separate community plugin ordered *before* `plugin-proposal-decorators` (legacy) in the customer's Babel config \u2014 that ordering/presence is the actual lever, since core Babel packages don't do it.\n\n**SWC side** (`swc--v1.4.6`):\n- `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` \u2014 `TransformConfig` struct, the exact surface for `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator` and `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata` (both `BoolConfig<false>` \u2014 off by default).\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/mod.rs` \u2014 `decorators(Config)` entry point; `c.legacy` picks the legacy TSC-style pass, and `c.emit_metadata` (wired from `decoratorMetadata`) gates whether metadata is emitted at all (the stage-3 path panics with `unimplemented!` if metadata is requested there).\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/legacy/mod.rs` \u2014 `TscDecorator`, SWC's parallel to Babel's `applyDecoratedDescriptor`; only runs `Metadata` visitor when `self.metadata` is true.\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/legacy/metadata.rs` \u2014 the actual `design:type`/`design:paramtypes`/`design:returntype` synthesis (SWC's `Reflect.metadata` analog, explicitly ported from `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata`).\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_typescript/src/typescript.rs` + `config.rs` \u2014 TS strip pass, confirming it runs type-erasure independent of the decorators pass, so type info must still be present when the decorators/metadata pass runs (ordering constraint mirrors the Babel plugin-order requirement).\n\n**Root cause**: NestJS DI needs both `legacyDecorator: true` **and** `decoratorMetadata: true` under `jsc.transform` in `.swcrc`. If the customer's config only set `legacyDecorator: true` (common when porting a Babel `legacy: true` setting) and left `decoratorMetadata` at its default `false`, `emit_metadata` stays false, the `Metadata` visitor in `legacy/metadata.rs` never runs, and no `design:type`/`design:paramtypes` decorators are ever attached \u2014 so `Reflect.getMetadata` returns `undefined` at Nest's IoC registration step, exactly matching the reported crash.",
